WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Did you know that

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.751
here in the Pacific Ocean,

00:00:01.751 --> 00:00:03.044
there's this huge

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:05.296
deposit of valuable metals?

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:06.047
Everyone agrees

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:07.048
that our future

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:08.633
is going to contain metals

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:09.384
like nickel,

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:10.135
cobalt,

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:10.802
copper

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:11.511
and manganese.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.095
These metals are

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:12.971
key ingredients

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:14.264
to making batteries,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:14.973
which we need

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:16.599
a lot of very soon

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:18.018
to get us away from

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:18.727
this.

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.769
Burning hydrocarbons

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:20.895
to move our bodies

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:21.521
and our goods

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.272
around the world.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:22.939
One way to get all

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:23.440
these metals

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:23.982
is to send

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:24.983
giant robots

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:25.608
to the bottom

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:26.609
of the ocean floor

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:27.610
to vacuum up

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:28.778
all of these deposits

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:29.612
and then to send them up

00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:30.947
to the ship on the surface.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:32.157
But there's one big problem,

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:32.657
which is that

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:34.451
this patch of ocean isn't

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:35.827
owned by any country.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.287
It's international waters.

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:37.871
So countries are going to

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.371
have to work together

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.748
and establish rules on

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:41.124
how to do this properly.

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:41.624
And at this point,

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:42.167
we don't know what

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:42.751
the environmental

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:43.626
implications are

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:44.753
of just digging up

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:45.628
all of these metals

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:46.796
from the bottom of the ocean.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:47.547
This is just one of

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.631
the many difficult trade-offs

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:49.716
that the world is facing

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.258
right now

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:51.634
as we figure out

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:52.552
solutions to this

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.344
climate crisis.

00:00:53.344 --> 00:00:54.304
If you want to better understand

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:55.138
global politics,

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:55.847
follow for more.

